{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoBranchPinnedB"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_nonvacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total_nonvacuous","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L513-L529","doc":"**Non-vacuity for `envelopeS_total`.** The conclusion is not a tautology\nabout an empty hypothesis set: a constant-plus-square `S` satisfies both\nhypotheses and the conclusion reads `π² = 0 + π²`.\n\nThe check with real content is Route 30, which measures `S′ = 2φ` on the actual\narc — per root to `4.6e-41` and summed to `9.2e-41`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS_total","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L501-L509","doc":"**The transport's total.** `envelope_integrate` applied to `S`, tolerating\none exceptional point — which is `φ₀`, where the discriminant vanishes and no\ndifferentiable root labelling exists (`exists_unit_circle_disc_zero`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fivetwo-envelope-transport","label":"prop:fivetwo-envelope-transport","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/fivetwo-envelope-transport.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_envelopeS","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L449-L497","doc":"**The transport's derivative.**\n\nThree envelope collapses, summed by `sum_dVdx_of_pinned`, evaluated by\n`envelope_value`. The two pinned log-sums `hA` and `hB` are hypotheses here and\ntheorems elsewhere (`logSumA_eq_log`, `logSumB_eq_neg_log`); the `Re(∂V/∂y·Y′)`\nconditions are the weakened envelope hypothesis, which is the one that is true\nat all three roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_neg_route","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_neg_route","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L416-L445","doc":"**Every root takes exactly one of the two `log(−y)` routes, and which one is\ndecided by the root alone.**\n\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS` needs `d/du log(−Yⱼ u)` and offers two ways to get it:\n`hasDerivAt_log_neg_of_slitPlane` when `−y` is off `log`'s cut, and\n`hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal` when it is on it. `−y ∈ slitPlane` unfolds to\n`Re y < 0 ∨ Im y ≠ 0`, so it fails **precisely** at a positive real `y`.\n\nNeither route is redundant. On this arc exactly one root is positive real at\nevery `φ` (`exists_root_mem_Ioo` puts it in `(0,1)`), so route 2 is needed\neverywhere and route 1 is impossible there — that is correction 6's fact, in the\nform a caller can use. The other two roots take route 1 either because they are\ngenuinely complex or, at the 46 arc points where all three roots are real,\nbecause they are negative (`real_root_neg_of_ne`).\n\n⚠ **This settles the routing, not the derivative.** Route 2's lemma is stated\nfor a path of the form `fun u => ((t u : ℝ) : ℂ)` — it needs `Y` to be\n*real-valued near `φ`*, not merely real *at* `φ`. That is a condition on the\nlabelling rather than on the root, so it belongs to the concrete `Y₁ Y₂ Y₃` still\nopen in `qou-glbl`. Stating the dichotomy here makes that the only thing left to\nsupply, instead of leaving both the routing and the path condition implicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_of_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_of_root","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L405-L414","doc":"**`VSide` in full, at every root of the curve on the OPEN arc.**\n\nAll six fields, no root structure, no labelling, no case analysis left to the\ncaller. `hxim : x.im ≠ 0` is the open-arc condition and it is load-bearing, not\ndecorative: at `φ = π` it is exactly what fails, and `VSide` fails with it\n(Route 36 G7). Proving this over `Icc 0 π` would be proving something false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L387-L403","doc":"**`y/x ∈ notCut` for every root on the open arc** — `VSide.hc₃`, in full.\n\n`mul_mem_notCut` at `x⁻¹`, via `curve_inv`. On `|x| = 1` the inverse has the same\nreal part and the negated imaginary part, so both hypotheses transport unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L366-L385","doc":"**`x·y ∈ notCut` for every root on the open arc** — `VSide.hc₂`, in full.\n\nThe disjunction, used as a disjunction. If `x·y` has nonzero imaginary part the\nfirst disjunct closes it. If it is real — which Route 36 G3 shows *does* happen,\nexactly once on `(0,π)`, contrary to that gate's retracted claim — then\n`quintic_of_mul_real` pins its value to a root of `r⁵ − r³ + 1` and\n`quintic_root_lt_one` puts that below `1`, closing the second.\n\nNote which fact does the work in each branch. For a *real* root the first\ndisjunct is elementary: `Im(x·y) = Im x · Re y`, nonzero on the open arc — and\nthat is exactly what expires at `φ = π`, taking `VSide` with it. The quintic is\nneeded only for the complex pair, at the one point where its `Im` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_inv","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L355-L364","doc":"**`x ↦ x⁻¹` is an involution of the curve**: `curve x⁻¹ y · x² = curve x y`.\n\nSo `x·y` and `y/x` are the *same* `Li₂` argument, read at `x` and at `x⁻¹` —\nand on `|x| = 1` the two points differ only by the sign of `Im x`. `hc₃` therefore\nneeds no argument of its own, and this is also why Route 36 G3 found the two\ncrossings at the same `φ` with the same value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_of_notCut_mul_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vSide_of_notCut_mul_div","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L334-L351","doc":"**`VSide` reduced to its two genuinely root-dependent fields.**\n\nGiven the two `notCut` memberships that need the labelling, the other four are\nsupplied. Stated this way so the residue is visible in a signature rather than in\nprose: what is left of `VSide` is `x·y` and `y/x` off the cut, nothing else.\n\nRoute 36 G3 measured both — they are carried by `Im ≠ 0` at every one of the 597\nchecks with `min |Im| = 0.00676`, a genuine margin and never a near-miss, so\nneither needs a case split of its own. `exists_pinning_data` already supplies\npart: `(x·y₃).im < 0`, and `(x·y₂).im < 0` once `c < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.quintic_root_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.quintic_root_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L309-L332","doc":"**No real root of `r⁵ − r³ + 1` reaches `1`** — because `r ≥ 1` forces\n`r⁵ − r³ + 1 = r³(r² − 1) + 1 ≥ 1 > 0`.\n\nThis quintic is not decoration. Route 36 G3 originally claimed that `x·y` is\n*never* real on the arc, so that `x·y ∈ notCut` would need no case split. That\nwas **false**, and the gate hid it by testing a grid minimum of `|Im(x·y)|`,\nwhich is not a lower bound: refining the grid shrank the minimum like `1/N`,\nthe signature of a zero crossing. There is exactly one crossing on `(0,π)`.\n\nAt it, `x·y` is real with value `r = −1.2365057033914990243`, and `r` is exactly\nthe unique real root of this quintic — with `c = r(1+r)/2` and `t = 1/r²`,\nmatching to 20 digits. It falls out of Vieta: if `x·y₂ = r` is real with\n`|x| = 1` then `y₂ = r·conj x`, so `y₃ = r·x`, and substituting into the curve\nmakes `x` a root of a cubic with **real** coefficients; `x` is non-real on the\nopen arc, so `conj x` is a root too and the third is `−r²`.\n\nSo `x·y ∈ notCut` at the crossing holds via `Re < 1` — the *opposite* disjunct\nfrom the retracted claim — and this lemma is what supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.quintic_of_mul_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.quintic_of_mul_real","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L255-L307","doc":"**If `x·y` is real on the arc, its value satisfies `r⁵ − r³ + 1 = 0`.**\n\nThis is the exact characterisation of Route 36 G3's crossing — the one the\nretracted G3 asserted could not happen. The derivation needs no Vieta and no\nroot tracking:\n\n* substituting `x·y = r` into `curve x y = 0` after multiplying by `x²` gives a\n  **cubic in `x` with real coefficients** (`r` is real);\n* on `|x| = 1` the quadratic `x² + 1 = 2·(Re x)·x` (`unitCircle_quadratic`) is\n  the minimal polynomial of a non-real `x` over `ℝ`, so that cubic reduces to\n  `α·x + β` with `α, β` **real** in `r` and `c = Re x`;\n* `x.im ≠ 0` then forces `α = 0` *and* `β = 0` — two real equations;\n* and `r⁵ − r³ + 1 = α + (r² + 2c)·β` identically.\n\n`hxim` is doing real work at the third step: without it the two coefficients\ncould trade off against each other, and indeed at `φ = 0` and `φ = π` — the\nexact points where `x.im = 0` — the conclusion fails, as it must, since `x·y` is\nreal there for *every* root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_mem_notCut_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_mem_notCut_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L243-L253","doc":"The `y/x` counterpart: `Im(y/x) = −Re y · Im x / ‖x‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_mem_notCut_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_mem_notCut_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L231-L241","doc":"For **real** `y ≠ 0` and `x` off the real axis, `Im(x·y) = Im x · Re y ≠ 0`.\n\nThis is what carries every *real* root on the **open** arc, with no case\nanalysis — and it is exactly what expires at `φ = π`, where `Im x = 0` and the\nroot `−2.2469796` is left with `Re(x·y) = 2.2469796` on the cut. See the `VSide`\ndocstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_root_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.div_root_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L227-L229","doc":"`y/x ≠ 0` at a root — `VSide.hn₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_root_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.mul_root_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L223-L225","doc":"`x·y ≠ 0` at a root — `VSide.hn₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.root_mem_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.root_mem_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L176-L221","doc":"**Every root of the curve on `|x| = 1` lies in `notCut`** — the real/complex\ncase split, discharged.\n\n`notCut = {w | Im w ≠ 0 ∨ Re w < 1}`. A root with `Im ≠ 0` takes the first\ndisjunct outright. A **real** root takes the second: on `|x| = 1` the `y`-cubic\nis `unitCubic (Re x)` with real coefficients, and no real root of that reaches\n`1` when `Re x ≤ 1` (`unitCubic_root_lt_one`).\n\n⚠ Both branches are live on the arc, so neither is defensive. Route 36 G5: the\narc crosses the discriminant at `c* = −0.74221766588`, giving **three** real\nroots at 46 of 199 sampled points and one real plus a conjugate pair at the other\n153. That is also why the real branch leans on `unitCubic_root_lt_one` — which\nbounds *every* real root — rather than on `exists_pinning_data`'s distinguished\n`t ∈ (0,1)`, which would leave two of the three unhandled at those 46 points.\n\n⚠ And the disjunct attribution here is the *exact* one, not the numerical one.\n`polyroots` returns `|Im| ~ 2.6e-41` for the real root at one arc point, so a\nsplit driven by a floating `Im ≠ 0` test would route that root through the first\ndisjunct — which is false in exact arithmetic, and is the branch this proof\ncannot take. Route 36 G2 classifies by root type for that reason.\n\n⚠ **`hx` is load-bearing — do not weaken it.** The statement reads as though it\nmight hold for general `x`, and it does not. The curve is *quadratic* in `x`, so\nfixing a bad `y` and solving produces a counterexample outright: at `y = 2` it is\n`2x² − 9x + 2 = 0`, giving `x = (9 ± √65)/4`, both real and neither on the unit\ncircle, with `y = 2` real and `Re y ≥ 1` — so `y ∉ notCut`. Route 36 G6 carries\nit exactly. `hx` is used twice and essentially: once for `curve_eq_unitCubic`,\nonce for `Re x ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.root_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.root_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L170-L174","doc":"**No root of the curve vanishes**, for `x ≠ 0`: `curve x 0 = −x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hn₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hn₃","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hn₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hn₂","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₃","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₂","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hc₁","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hy0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.hy0","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.VSide","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L113-L154","doc":"The side conditions under which `V` is differentiable at `(x, y)`: each\n`Li₂` argument off the cut `[1,∞)` and nonzero. Bundled so the main statement\nstays readable.\n\n⚠ `−y ∈ slitPlane` is deliberately **absent**. An earlier draft included it, and\nRoute 31 G4 showed that made the whole statement **vacuous at the positive real\nroot** — which on this arc is one of the three roots at every `φ`. The `log(−y)`\nderivative is passed separately instead, by whichever of\n`hasDerivAt_log_neg_of_slitPlane` / `hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal` applies.\n\n## ⚠⚠ `VSide` is FALSE at `φ = π`. Prove it over `Ico 0 π`, never `Icc 0 π`.\n\nRoute 36 G7. At the endpoint `x = −1` the three roots are the level-7 roots and\nare **all real**, so for each of them `Im(x·y) = y·sin φ` vanishes — every\nimaginary part goes at once. Two are still carried by `Re < 1`; the third,\n`y = −2.2469796`, gives `x·y = +2.2469796`, real with `Re ≥ 1`. That is exactly\nLi₂'s cut, so `hc₂` and `hc₃` fail there. Attempting `VSide` on the closed\ninterval is attempting something false.\n\nThe transport is **unaffected**, and it is worth seeing why rather than\nassuming it: `envelopeS_total` asks for `ContinuousOn … (Icc 0 π)` but for\n`HasDerivAt` only on `Ico 0 π`. The endpoint needs a *value*, not\ndifferentiability — and `sum_re_deformedV_at_neg_one` already supplies that\nvalue at `x = −1`, with no differentiability hypothesis anywhere in it. So the\ntwo results meet exactly at the point where this one has to stop.\n\n`hasDerivAt_envelopeS` below carries `hhi : φ ≤ π` for `arcX_arg`'s principal\nrange. That is not wrong — the theorem holds — but at `φ = π` its `VSide`\nhypotheses cannot be met by the actual roots, so it has no instance there.\n\n⚠ And this is invisible to a naive check. `exp(I * π)` evaluates to\n`−1 + 4.1e-43·I`, and that spurious imaginary part satisfies `notCut`'s first\ndisjunct, so a numerical probe reports the endpoint as fine. Route 36 G7 builds\n`x = −1` exactly for that reason — the same trap `root_mem_notCut` documents,\nin a second place. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelopeS","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L107-L111","doc":"**`S(φ) = Σⱼ Re V(x φ, yⱼ φ)`.** The three root-paths are parameters; see\nthe module docstring for why they are not constructed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_arg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L101-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_arcX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_arcX","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L96-L99","doc":"`log(e^{iφ}) = iφ` on the principal branch, for `φ ∈ (−π, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L92-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_im","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L89-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_re","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_arcX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_arcX","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L78-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arcX","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoTransport.lean#L73-L74","doc":"The transport path `x(φ) = e^{iφ}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}